.TH CUDDLE-GUI 1 "2026-11-04" "cuddle 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cuddle-gui \- offline Litmo room hub
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cuddle-gui
.RI [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
GTK4 and Qt6 builds offer the shared libcuddle rooms, including touch mapping,
conflict practice, want-or-should questions, flood, morning and aftercare.
The HTML backend remains a local Soft Signal STOP page.
.SH CONTROLS
Use the mouse or keyboard to select rooms and choices.
q or Escape stops immediately. Stopped sessions never resume automatically.
Larger, quieter view increases text size. No answers are stored or sent.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cuddle (1),
.BR cuddle-tui (1)

.SH PREFERENCES
The GTK Preferences screen (Ctrl+comma) previews display settings.
Save preferences explicitly writes appearance, text size, theme and starting
room only. Back to rooms discards an unsaved preview. Room answers are never
saved. Opening Preferences ends the current room.
Alt+Home returns to rooms; Alt+Left goes back a step; Page Up/Down scrolls.
